<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raja Kecil</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1746">1746</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raja Kecil was a Minangkabau-backed adventurer who claimed to be the posthumous son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-shah-ii-of-johor">Mahmud Shah II of Johor</a>. In 1718 he seized the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a> throne, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> forces drove him out in 1722. He then founded the Siak Sultanate on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>'s east coast, which became a leading Malay power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raja-kecil.jpg" alt="Raja Kecil" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harris Est 13 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jirat_Makam_Marhum_Buantan.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
